WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.980
'80s nostalgia is in the air, so no wonder
the ninth season of American Horror Story

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.720
is taking place smack dab in the middle of
that decade.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.200
But how will AHS 1984 fit into the show's
ever-expanding canon?

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.480
Here's everything we know so far.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.880
Leave it to AHS co-creator Ryan Murphy to
blend '80s camp with the menacing undertones

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.500
of a slasher film - and all set to the kicky
tune of Dan Hartman's "I Can Dream About You."

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.960
Back in July 2019, Murphy made the official
cast announcement on Instagram through a series

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:30.760
of stylish videos staged to look like "camera
tests."

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.519
As you can see, everyone is decked out in
their most ill-advised '80s fashions.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.840
Hard to say whether this is what the cast
will actually look like throughout the coming

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:38.340
season.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.480
They could just be toying with our expectations
here.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.340
Meanwhile, the official teaser trailers heavily
draw from slasher-film archetypes and scenarios.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.200
In one teaser, we see a truck full of youngsters
on their way to Camp Redwood.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.010
They're partying so hard they fail to see
the word "BEWARE" scrawled in red paint on

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.699
the back of the "Camp Redwood" sign.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.500
Meanwhile, a masked man with a knife is hiding
in the undercarriage.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.820
This guy really gets around: He later jumps
out of a lake in order to stab a bikini-clad

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.440
woman - basically a straight-up homage to
the first Friday the 13th.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.580
In another teaser, a young woman is chased
through the dark woods.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.840
She hides in a cabin, and soon enough, a knife
comes through the door.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.780
Yet another teaser features a group of camp
counselors settling into their bunks.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.280
And when the cabin door closes?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.060
Another teaser demonstrates the dangers of
skinny dipping:

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:25.800
“ah”

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.780
And this teaser is an ode to the simple pleasures
like listening to your Walkman, and getting

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:30.740
brutally murdered.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:32.960
“ah”

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.080
Our theory?

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.380
This season is going to be a whole lot of
fun.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.280
As with previous seasons of American Horror
Story, Ryan Murphy has assembled a mix of

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.980
new and returning cast members to play all-new
characters, this time in 1984.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.560
Returning stars include Cody Fern, Billie
Lourd, Emma Roberts, Leslie Grossman, and

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.940
a decidedly creepy John Carroll Lynch.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.119
We're particularly loving Cody Fern as an
'80s-style preppy dude... especially since

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.220
he looks a bit like James Spader in Pretty
in Pink.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.590
Newcomers include Olympic skier Gus Kenworthy,
Glee alum Matthew Morrison, Angelica Ross

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:09.280
from the hit series Pose, Dear White People's
DeRon Horton, and actor and musician Zach

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:09.840
Villa.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.060
Unfortunately, AHS 1984 will be losing some
of the series' most beloved cast members,

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.560
too.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.620
You know how that goes.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.180
"What is this?

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.780
Knotty pine!"

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.980
Of course, Jessica Lange left the show as
a regular player after the fourth season,

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.040
Freak Show… and now two more regulars are
following in her footsteps.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.920
Sadly, Evan Peters won't be returning this
season.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.400
Due to the intensity of his roles in both
American Horror Story and Ryan Murphy's Pose,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.600
he decided to take a break.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.860
Meanwhile, Sarah Paulson won't be returning
to the show in any significant role, although

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.120
Deadline reports we can expect to see her
at some point in the season.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.340
With any luck, she'll pop up in a cameo like
Lange did in Season 8.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.000
In the upcoming season of AHS, '80s nostalgia
in clearly in full bloom, so it might be worth

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.970
revisiting some seminal horror films from
1984 - just in case Ryan Murphy has decided

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.380
to use them for inspiration.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.220
1984 was a big year for the horror genre.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.120
After all, that was the year A Nightmare on
Elm Street was released.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.600
"Hey, Nancy… no running in the hallways."

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.860
Then there was Friday the 13th: The Final
Chapter.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.720
And who can forget Children of the Corn?

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:19.960
"Stop him!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.400
Kill him!"

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.100
"MALACHAI!"

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.820
Also worth noting: Firestarter came out in
1984, and so did Brian DePalma's campy psychological

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:32.900
thriller Body Double.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.840
Both films certainly align with Murphy's unique
brand of horror.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:41.120
Then again, longtime AHS executive producer
Tim Minear reminds us to expect the unexpected.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.760
TheWrap asked whether this season would be
revisiting '80s horror films, and he replied:

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.319
"Generally, Ryan is ahead of the zeitgeist
as opposed to following it.

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:52.480
So what I would say is that this has been
an area that Ryan has talked about since I’ve

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.640
known him and it’s just a real sweet spot
for him.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.520
And I think it was time for him to do it."

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.760
So what's the story?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.879
It looks like AHS 1984 is going to be a beautiful,
gory, and funny homage to the slasher films

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:05.640
of the '80s.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.280
But this is a Ryan Murphy production, so you
can probably expect some social and political

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.000
subtext, too.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.320
After all, the year 1984 corresponds to George
Orwell's dystopian novel of the same name.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.140
Just sayin'.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.640
One more thing: The use of The Motel's classic
single "Suddenly Last Summer" in the "Camp

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.920
Redwood" teaser could be a clue to the plotline.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.760
After all, Suddenly, Last Summer is a classic
1958 play written by Tennessee Williams.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.120
It was later adapted into a film starring
Elizabeth Taylor.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.160
The story involves a woman named Catharine
who's traumatized after witnessing her cousin's

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:36.660
death.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:41.600
Her aunt - played by Katherine Hepburn - attempts
to keep her son's death a secret by lobotomizing

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.100
her niece.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.080
It's some pretty melodramatic stuff.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:48.120
"I ran, they let me run, they didn't even
see me…"

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.740
It also covers subject matter that's up this
series' alley, and we wouldn't be at all surprised

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:56.680
if the show pays homage to Suddenly, Last
Summer in AHS 1984.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:02.390
The ninth season of American Horror Story
premieres on September 18th, 2019 at 10pm

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:03.000
Eastern time.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:07.340
The season will have a ten-episode run, with
the seventh episode set to air on October

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.820
30th… which just so happens to be Halloween
Eve.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.340
How terribly apropos.

